            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0387" n="1221" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/315</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-16T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7313. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 355. Your No. 416, Embassy No. 9475, April 12, 11 p.m. We have been forcing
                    vessels proceeding to the Plate to load coal for the railways and other purposes
                    so that there has accumulated large tonnage of general cargo, which tends to
                    congest railways and shipping terminals. We are being urged by Argentina to
                    pursue a more liberal policy in exports to Argentina. Swedish vessels proceeding
                    direct would make small saving in time; but would require bunkers from stations
                    where Allied tonnage has been used for coal transportation instead of from
                    American ports. We seriously object to Swedish vessels proceeding in ballast,
                    which results in an economic, as well as tonnage waste. We nevertheless leave
                    the matter in your hands for final determination.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
